2026-07-05 17:17:08.470 | INFO     | app.services.set_service:get_text_for_set:244 - [GET TEXT] Final result text: On quiet Sundays, I wander through the old market and enjoy simple leisure.  
My neighbor and I retrieve fresh bread before the town becomes busy.  
We often employ these walks as a small endeavor to clear our minds.  
The air feels wholesome, and every corner invites us to wander longer.  
At the river, I retrieve stones for my collection while birds wander above.  
These moments of leisure help me employ patience in a noisy week.  
My brother joins the endeavor, and together we wander home with warm tea.  
We retrieve forgotten stories from the past, making the afternoon feel wholesome.  
Even small errands become a pleasant leisure when we employ a calm pace.  
By evening, I wander back satisfied, knowing this simple endeavor was worthwhile.
